# Input
```js
/* should generate diagnostics */
import { ref } from 'vue'
const count = ref(0)
;(() => {
	const value1 = count.value
})()
;(function () {
	const value2 = count.value
})()
;(() => {
	;(() => {
		const value3 = count.value
	})()
})()

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid-iife.js:5:17 lint/nursery/noVueRefObjectReactivityLoss ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! This reads the value of a ref only once, so it won't update when the ref changes.
  
    3 │ const count = ref(0)
    4 │ ;(() => {
  > 5 │ 	const value1 = count.value
      │ 	               ^^^^^^^^^^^
    6 │ })()
    7 │ ;(function () {
  
  i This code runs only once, together with the code that creates the ref. The value read here is a copy, and Vue does not update it when the ref changes.
  
  i Read .value inside a function, such as a computed() getter, or pass the ref itself instead of its value.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

